        "narrative": "<p>East Pike Lake supports good numbers of fast-growing northern pike and smallmouth bass, with some large individuals present.  The northern pike population is apparently a \"booming\" population, as only one fish captured during any other DNR assessment of this lake has been identified as a northern pike (1989).Anglers report catching muskellunge as recently as 1998, and muskellunge fry were stocked in 1977, but only one fish captured during any DNR assessment has been identified as a muskellunge.    East Pike Lake is within the Boundary Waters Canoe Area Wilderness, and angling pressure is probably fairly light.</p>",
